Make the ZIP reader refuse four hostile archives it accepted or hung on,
and find the central directory behind a long archive comment.

Only the archive build compiles this code (libzukomp.a's miniz_zip.o);
every hunk is under MINIZ_NO_ARCHIVE_APIS, so zukomp.so is unchanged.
Found by fuzz_zip_reader and tools/check-zip-reader.py (zukomp #37, #92).

1. mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_read() hung on an archive opened from memory
   when a deflated member's DEFLATE stream ended before its final block.
   In memory mode comp_remaining is never decremented, so
   TINFL_FLAG_HAS_MORE_INPUT stayed set and tinfl answered "needs more
   input" forever. From memory there is never more input than the buffer.

2. mz_zip_reader_extract_to_mem() read a stored entry's uncompressed size
   from its data offset. When that exceeds the compressed size it reads
   past the entry's data, into whatever follows, and succeeds if the
   CRC-32 matches the over-read. mz_zip_reader_read_central_dir() means to
   refuse such an entry, but reads the method with MZ_READ_LE32, method
   and modification time as one word, so it does only at DOS time 0. The
   entry is refused where it is extracted, as the iterator and
   extract_to_callback already do, rather than widening what opening an
   archive refuses.

3. A DEFLATE stream tinfl refused, in any of the three extraction paths,
   and extract_to_mem's output running past the declared size, failed
   with the last error still MZ_ZIP_NO_ERROR. They now say why.

4. extract_to_mem and extract_to_callback returned success for an entry
   with no compressed data before checking anything else: a non-empty
   CRC-32, or a ZIP64 entry declaring a non-zero uncompressed size, which
   left the caller's buffer unwritten. The iterator refused both.

5. mz_zip_reader_locate_header_sig() stepped its scan window back with
   cur_file_ofs - (sizeof(buf_u32) - 3), which is unsigned: under one
   window it wrapped, the next read went past the end and failed, and a
   valid archive whose EOCD sat more than 4 KiB from the end but in its
   first 4 KiB (a long archive comment) was refused as having no central
   directory. Forming that pointer is also undefined behaviour, which
   UBSan reports on any such non-archive input.

Upstream (richgel999/miniz master) has the same code at the time of
writing.

